Step 2 of the build-up. Identical to
cloud-vms-vs-containers-what-customers-buy-1.svg (see that prompt), with
nothing moved, plus the reality behind the three orders:

- One physical host operated by the cloud provider, wrapping everything.
- A dashed "Container platform" area around B's and C's workloads, labelled
  "rents one VM per customer".
- A VM box around B's containers and another around C's containers, each
  labelled "Platform VM" / "B only" resp. "C only". Never two customers in
  one VM.
- Bottom layers across all VMs: host kernel + KVM (one VMM process per VM,
  e.g. Cloud Hypervisor), then hardware.
- The footer becomes: "Where it actually runs: every customer ends up in a VM
  of their own."

The VMs stay empty here except for the containers from step 1; their contents
follow in step 3.
